WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:02.190
- Welcome to another
episode off Firm Learning.

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:04.050
Hope you're all doing great.

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:05.900
And today I want to talk about something

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.760
that has been on my mind
for quite some time,

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.640
and it's based on many messages

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:13.890
I get from you on Instagram, on LinkedIn,

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:14.910
on all the socials.

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:16.960
And I think that this is really something

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.730
where many of you just
have a mindset problem,

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:21.364
very frankly, right?

00:00:21.364 --> 00:00:22.370
I think many of you're getting this wrong.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:25.230
So it's going to be a little
bit like a real talk format,

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.070
a little bit of a rant, maybe.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:30.360
So I hope you can apologize
me for doing that.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.000
But I trust it's going to be fine, okay?

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.250
And the issue that I have,

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:35.160
what many of you're doing,

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.537
is that you're writing
messages saying things like,

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:40.917
"Oh I want to join consulting,
what do I need to do?

00:00:40.917 --> 00:00:43.237
"I'm still maybe even
a high school student.

00:00:43.237 --> 00:00:46.137
"And I just want to do everything
to get into consulting.

00:00:46.137 --> 00:00:47.467
"What do I need to study?

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:49.494
"What extracurriculars do I need to do?"

00:00:49.494 --> 00:00:52.350
Also, another thing that
I get very regularly,

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:54.472
is people who are already in their careers

00:00:54.472 --> 00:00:56.260
for a couple of years,

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:58.050
maybe you work in big four,

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.580
maybe in industry, maybe somewhere else.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:02.207
And then I get message saying,

00:01:02.207 --> 00:01:05.807
"I wanna get into McKinsey
into BCG, into Bain.

00:01:05.807 --> 00:01:07.207
"I want to do an MBA,

00:01:07.207 --> 00:01:10.247
"or should I do an MBA
to get into these firms?

00:01:10.247 --> 00:01:12.379
"Is this what will get me in?"

00:01:12.379 --> 00:01:13.212
Right?

00:01:13.212 --> 00:01:14.887
And then, "What program do I need to do?

00:01:14.887 --> 00:01:16.707
"Where do I need to study," and so on,

00:01:16.707 --> 00:01:18.220
"to fulfill this goal?"

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:21.190
And I think there are many problems

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:24.890
with this type of mindset
and type of attitude,

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:27.050
because I think the reality is just,

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:28.520
especially if you have the goal,

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:31.060
to go into firms like McKinsey, BCG, Bain,

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:32.360
I mean, just stay with that.

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:34.516
These are three firms, three firms.

00:01:34.516 --> 00:01:37.840
And I know that, of course
they're quite prestigious.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:40.830
I know that many people
want to get into them.

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:43.390
And of course I think there
are good reasons for that.

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:44.350
And of course on my channel,

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:46.840
I talk about many of these reasons.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.860
But there can be so many reasons why,

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:52.330
even if you make it into the interviews,

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:53.960
that you do not get in.

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:55.920
Surely there's, I would argue,

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.820
quite a high rate of
false negatives, right?

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:02.400
So people who probably
would've deserved to get in,

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.368
but just didn't make
it through the process,

00:02:04.368 --> 00:02:06.850
maybe because they
didn't have the best day,

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:08.420
maybe the chemistry,

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:11.910
with with one or the other
interviewer didn't work out well.

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:15.830
There are things that you
cannot always influence, right?

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:17.110
And you need to live with that.

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:18.640
That's life.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:21.030
So, but if this is what's happening,

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:23.248
how can you think that it's a good idea,

00:02:23.248 --> 00:02:26.950
to just structure your whole
life, your whole adolescence,

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:28.160
your whole twenties,

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.630
around getting into these three firms?

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:32.540
Frankly, I think that's
a little bit childish.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:35.150
Frankly, I do not think
it makes a lot of sense.

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:39.050
I do not think that this is a
smart decision to do, right?

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:41.750
And let's further deep dive into that,

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:43.930
because of course there
are lots of decisions

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.340
that are are attached to that.

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:47.800
And it starts already in your undergrad.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:48.687
You're asking yourself,

00:02:48.687 --> 00:02:50.967
"What degree should I study,

00:02:50.967 --> 00:02:54.690
"to get into MBB, get
into McKenzie, BCG, Bain?"

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:55.523
I mean, come on.

00:02:55.523 --> 00:02:56.960
This shouldn't be the only reason, right?

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:00.510
So you pick a degree
subject only for that?

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:03.000
But then what if you
happen, if you realize,

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.200
that you don't get in?

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.570
Then all these years were wasted?

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:08.100
How does that make sense?

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.580
And even if you do make
it, if you do get in in

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:12.820
just the truth that on average,

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:16.490
a consultant probably stays
for two, three, four years

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:17.728
at any of these firms.

00:03:17.728 --> 00:03:20.660
So for such a short amount of time,

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:22.979
you want to make these
important decisions?

00:03:22.979 --> 00:03:26.170
Again, I do not think this makes sense.

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:28.870
Next step, for the MBA.

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:30.600
People are considering,

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.310
this at least the impression that I get

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:33.840
from many of your messages,

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:37.190
people are considering to do an MBA,

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:41.750
to spend often a six digital
amount of money in tuition,

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:44.440
in living costs, and foregone salary,

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:49.440
just to get into MBB, or
to hope to get into MBB,

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:53.310
because what happens if you
then don't get in, in the end?

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:54.300
And frankly, while of course,

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.860
I hope that everyone who does an MBA,

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:57.570
also for fulfills these goats,

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:01.090
and I do think that doing
MBA might be a great avenue

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:02.810
into these career paths.

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:04.750
I also just know from
my personal experience

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:06.850
having done the MBA at NSEAD,

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:08.030
that there are many people

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:10.837
who hoped to get into this
level of MBB consulting,

00:04:10.837 --> 00:04:13.940
and then for different
reasons, didn't make it.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:15.730
Was it then all for nothing?

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:19.910
Did you just spend all
this money, all this time,

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:21.510
for not meeting your goals?

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:23.863
Is this really how you want
to think about your life?

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:27.280
I really think this is not a healthy way

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:29.140
to look at these types of things.

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:30.830
It's not a mature way, I would say.

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:32.629
It's a little bit childish, frankly.

00:04:32.629 --> 00:04:36.100
And I think it's absolutely
fair to say you have a goal,

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.720
that you want to get into consulting,

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:40.740
that you'd love to also
get into MBB consulting.

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:42.750
And yes, I would argue
probably there is a difference

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:46.015
between tier one, tier two,
tier three consulting firms.

00:04:46.015 --> 00:04:49.010
But surely you shouldn't obsess

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:50.950
around this being your only goal.

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:54.460
You shouldn't plan your whole
life around that, right?

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.293
And of course

00:04:55.293 --> 00:04:56.780
many things you do,

00:04:56.780 --> 00:04:59.720
that will help you to
potentially get into MBB,

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:00.553
will also help you

00:05:00.553 --> 00:05:03.570
to get into other attractive career paths.

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:06.320
So it's about your GPA, the grades,

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:09.700
if you write good grades,
a strong GPA, of course,

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:11.040
this will help you in
other things as well.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.350
If you work on the
extracurriculars, and so on.

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:16.183
But don't do things only because you hope

00:05:16.183 --> 00:05:18.190
that this will help you to do it.

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:21.010
You shouldn't do an MBA
if your own objective

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:23.870
to get into MBB, because chances
are on the end of the day,

00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:26.620
quiet high that you won't make it.

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:29.380
So let's talk about some other
things that you could do,

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:31.677
that are very attractive.

00:05:31.677 --> 00:05:34.150
A couple of ideas, maybe also for you,

00:05:34.150 --> 00:05:36.130
if you really feel like the only way

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:39.230
for you to have a great
career in management,

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:42.540
and general management, is
to do McKinsey, BCG, Bain,

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:43.373
What else could you do?

00:05:43.373 --> 00:05:46.010
What might be great alternatives?

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:48.540
First idea: fund a startup.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:52.280
I have actually many people
I personally studied with,

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:54.950
in my time here at University of Munich,

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:59.028
that instead of starting a
career in McKinsey, BCG, Bain,

00:05:59.028 --> 00:06:00.240
tier one consulting

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:03.660
they founded a startup,
and now have unicorns.

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:05.990
And probably it was a golden time,

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:07.790
especially also in the last years.

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:10.200
But again, several people I studied with,

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:13.300
who were in my semester, in my cohort,

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:16.130
who founded now today, unicorns.

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:19.222
And surely, these people do not regret

00:06:19.222 --> 00:06:22.091
to have not joined MBB in the end, right?

00:06:22.091 --> 00:06:24.380
And of course not everyone makes it.

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:25.430
Survivorship bias,

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:28.040
many people who started
startups, who didn't do it.

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:30.590
But I think in the end of the
day, it's much more realistic,

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:34.300
much more possible, than
maybe you think, first point.

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:35.510
Second point,

00:06:35.510 --> 00:06:38.620
if you maybe you feel like it's
too much to risk to do that,

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:41.690
to start your own startup,
join such a startup,

00:06:41.690 --> 00:06:44.220
join such a young company, right?

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:47.180
So join a startup that
is already established.

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:48.840
I think the sweet spot probably

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:53.840
is to join a company that just
raised a serious A, right?

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:57.917
So that just raised a big
substantial financing round,

00:06:57.917 --> 00:06:59.780
because of what this means is

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:01.980
that the company already does show

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:03.740
some level of traction,

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:07.860
does at least show initial
signs of product market fit.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:10.730
So you take out a lot of the initial risk

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:12.460
of joining such a company.

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:14.160
You are in a situation where the company

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:16.201
now raised significant amounts of money.

00:07:16.201 --> 00:07:19.097
Good, serious A rounds
today are often 10, 20, 30,

00:07:19.097 --> 00:07:20.920
$40 million.

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:23.800
If you look at the last
valuations, the current numbers.

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:25.190
So these are often environments

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:27.100
where lots of people get hired,

00:07:27.100 --> 00:07:28.620
where you might suddenly be in a position,

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:31.550
even as a junior person
who is doing a good job,

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:33.690
to only, after aa short amount of time,

00:07:33.690 --> 00:07:36.771
to become a team lead, to
become lots of responsibility.

00:07:36.771 --> 00:07:39.865
And I think people also
severely underestimate

00:07:39.865 --> 00:07:44.180
the salaries that you can
earn in these type of roles.

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:46.270
Frankly, I think in these environments,

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:49.400
for these fast hyper
growth type of companies,

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:52.870
you can often earn salaries
absolutely equivalent

00:07:52.870 --> 00:07:56.160
to people being consultants,
senior consultants,

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:59.102
even project leads, in
consulting type of environments.

00:07:59.102 --> 00:08:02.240
And often of course, the
lifestyle is significantly better,

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:06.010
than what you can expect
at McKinsey, BCG Bain.

00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:07.550
And frankly, if you would be interested

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:09.006
in an opportunity like that,

00:08:09.006 --> 00:08:12.260
we have currently a role like
that at my current employer,

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:15.090
at my current company
Building Radar, as well.

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:19.150
We are looking for a role that
we call a revenue engineer.

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:20.550
So Building Radar is doing something

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:22.400
that is called revenue engineering.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:25.570
We are helping industry
and construction companies,

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:28.388
to digitalize, and fuel their sales,

00:08:28.388 --> 00:08:30.700
and commercial processes.

00:08:30.700 --> 00:08:33.383
And we are hiring at the moment
for this one specific role.

00:08:33.383 --> 00:08:36.245
It will be a role that
very closely works together

00:08:36.245 --> 00:08:38.160
with us as a C level,

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:40.630
So me, including with the
board of Building Radar,

00:08:40.630 --> 00:08:43.270
with the managing directors
of Building Radar.

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:45.920
It is a role where you
will work closely together

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:48.438
with some of our largest customers,

00:08:48.438 --> 00:08:52.010
with senior leadership
of large industry players

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:53.620
in Germany, and in Europe.

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:55.030
And it is a position

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:57.320
where you can have a significant influence

00:08:57.320 --> 00:09:00.608
on the strategic direction
of our young company.

00:09:00.608 --> 00:09:02.690
So if this would be something

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:04.560
that you would be interested in,

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:07.020
I will leave a link to this job posting

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:08.290
in the video description.

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:09.302
Check it out.

00:09:09.302 --> 00:09:10.860
Two requirements though:

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:13.014
first you need to be based in Munich.

00:09:13.014 --> 00:09:15.600
So it's not a fully remote position.

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:17.396
And second, you need to be fluent

00:09:17.396 --> 00:09:19.780
both in English and in German.

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:21.007
But if you meet these requirements,

00:09:21.007 --> 00:09:24.495
you can apply via the link
in the video description.

00:09:24.495 --> 00:09:26.390
Just also write in your cover letter,

00:09:26.390 --> 00:09:27.890
that you saw this video.

00:09:27.890 --> 00:09:29.700
And then I would also have the opportunity

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:31.310
to look at your application this way.

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:33.664
And frankly, I think another benefit

00:09:33.664 --> 00:09:35.040
of joining such a position
in the young company,

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:37.821
is that I think there's
no better preparation,

00:09:37.821 --> 00:09:40.770
to eventually found your own startup.

00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:42.700
If you maybe don't wanna do it right away,

00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:43.660
out of university,

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:45.418
with a couple of years of work experience.

00:09:45.418 --> 00:09:46.327
There's no better way

00:09:46.327 --> 00:09:49.798
than having worked for such
a young growth company,

00:09:49.798 --> 00:09:52.050
because all the things that you see,

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:54.270
that you learn with
working together closely

00:09:54.270 --> 00:09:56.550
with the management
team, with the founders,

00:09:56.550 --> 00:09:58.405
these will be exactly the learnings,

00:09:58.405 --> 00:10:02.590
that will help you to then
start your own venture as well,

00:10:02.590 --> 00:10:06.200
raise capital, raise money,
and bring that to life.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:09.240
And then the third overarching
opportunity that I see

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:12.430
as an alternative to what
you can do in consulting,

00:10:12.430 --> 00:10:14.980
is B2B sales.

00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:17.350
This is also something that I
learned over the last years.

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:20.090
I think it's absolutely crazy,

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:24.504
the careers that people have
work as an account executive

00:10:24.504 --> 00:10:26.790
as a key account manager,

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:30.720
for any of these B2B sales companies.

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:31.930
Here behind us, actually,

00:10:31.930 --> 00:10:36.130
there's the office of
Salesforce here in Munich.

00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:38.170
If you are, are an account executive,

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:39.820
at a company like Salesforce,

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:41.470
and that's just one of many examples.

00:10:41.470 --> 00:10:44.350
So any of these SaaS companies, and again,

00:10:44.350 --> 00:10:45.440
including Building Radar,

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:47.830
because we are SaaS company as well,

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:52.830
the people there can earn
easily six digit salaries,

00:10:52.957 --> 00:10:56.686
just a great career sets,
lots of opportunities,

00:10:56.686 --> 00:10:59.316
also lots of growth
potential that you see.

00:10:59.316 --> 00:11:02.380
So if working together with B2B customers,

00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:06.900
if working together with other
people, selling products,

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:08.030
in the B2B environment,

00:11:08.030 --> 00:11:09.580
is something that you're interested in,

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:12.090
think about pursuing
such a career in sales,

00:11:12.090 --> 00:11:13.110
because the truth is,

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:15.360
salaries are probably rather comparable

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:16.569
to what you can expect

00:11:16.569 --> 00:11:20.142
in the first three to
five years in consulting.

00:11:20.142 --> 00:11:24.440
Plus the work/life balance
is significantly better,

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:26.130
to what you can expect in consulting.

00:11:26.130 --> 00:11:28.570
And again, then from such
a safe leadership position

00:11:28.570 --> 00:11:30.090
that you will be eventually in.

00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:30.923
This, of course,

00:11:30.923 --> 00:11:33.480
is surely also great than
development step point

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:35.360
to then also move into other areas,

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:38.870
into other leadership positions
of the company overall.

00:11:38.870 --> 00:11:39.703
And then potentially,

00:11:39.703 --> 00:11:43.230
of course also starting your
own business in the end.

00:11:43.230 --> 00:11:44.250
So I hope this makes sense to you.

00:11:44.250 --> 00:11:46.130
Yes, I am still

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:48.640
and I will continue to be a
big proponent of consulting.

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:50.840
I think it is a great start your career.

00:11:50.840 --> 00:11:53.540
I think spending a few
years at McKinsey, BCG,

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:55.330
any of these companies,

00:11:55.330 --> 00:11:57.370
rarely you did anything
back to anyone, right?

00:11:57.370 --> 00:11:59.760
So I think really it's of
course a great opportunity,

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:03.110
but don't get stuck up on
joining of these firms.

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:06.999
Think of alternatives, think
of the options that you have.

00:12:06.999 --> 00:12:10.680
Don't develop your profile
too closely, too narrowly,

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:14.240
towards such a thing which
maybe might work out,

00:12:14.240 --> 00:12:16.280
or might not work out for you in the end.

00:12:16.280 --> 00:12:18.930
And again, in any ways
for almost all people,

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:20.980
there will be a career after consulting.

00:12:20.980 --> 00:12:22.770
Only very few people stay there

00:12:22.770 --> 00:12:24.660
until the partner role.

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:26.470
It's very unlikely that
you would do that as well.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:28.540
And that alone should
be reason enough for you

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:31.440
to then find your own position,
to find your own path.

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:32.273
So thank you.

00:12:32.273 --> 00:12:34.150
This is just what I wanted
to talk about today.

00:12:34.150 --> 00:12:35.310
Appreciate your time.

